## AI Knowledge Base Enforcement

This repo keeps a living knowledge base in `.ai/`. These rules apply to every session.

### Before every commit or PR - mandatory assessment

| File | Update when |
|------|-------------|
| `.ai/plans/status.md` | **Always** - reflect current in-flight, blocked, and recently completed work |
| `.ai/memory.md` | Module structure, public interfaces, data model, or release state changed |
| `.ai/specs/01-architecture.md` | A module was added, the data model changed, or a key decision was made |
| `.ai/specs/dataflow.md` | How data moves through the system changed |
| `.ai/specs/product-spec.md` | A feature shipped, got blocked, or was descoped |
| `.claude/agents/` | A subagent's scope, tool allowlist, or model tier changed |
| `.ai/standards/` | Testing or code discipline changed |

### PR creation

Always use the `/creating-pr` skill (`.claude/skills/creating-pr/SKILL.md`) when
opening a PR. Never skip the `.ai/` assessment. Never open a PR without updating
`.ai/plans/status.md`.

### Available subagents (`.claude/agents/`)

Opus is never a minion. Each agent reads `crow` and this repo's namespace through
its own fenced `brain` server, and writes only the `minions` scratch namespace.

| Agent | Tier | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `repo-scout` | haiku | Mechanical search and inventory: every place X appears, file listings, counts. |
| `security-reviewer` | sonnet | Secrets, PII, unguarded paths, destructive writes without a backup. Run before every commit that touches credentials or path handling. |
| `ai-docs-auditor` | sonnet | Audits `.ai/` against the code and reports drift as `path:line`. Run before every PR. |
| `researcher` | sonnet | Read-only research across the repo and the public web, findings with sources. No shell: `gh`, `git` and authenticated APIs stay on the main thread. |

Never use the built-in `general-purpose` agent for minion work: it carries the
Agent tool and the main thread's model. Pick one of the agents above and name its
tier. A minion that tries to spawn its own is denied by `gingugu hook tool`.

### Forks: parallel hard work

Opus work - design, tests for an unsettled design, debugging - is never handed to
a cold minion. When there is more than one thread of it, **fork**: the Agent tool
with `subagent_type: "fork"` (or `/subtask`). A fork inherits the whole
conversation, system prompt and model, so it is a branch of the main thread, not
a briefing; `gingugu hook tool` gives it the main thread's rights. Pass
`isolation: "worktree"` when it writes files. A fork cannot fork again.

Split hard parallel work across forks, let each one design and write the tests,
and approve its verdict on the main thread. Once a design is settled, its
implementation goes to a Sonnet minion working against those tests.

### Logs

Hook events are logged as JSON lines in `logs/*.jsonl` - metadata only (tool,
path, decision), never file contents, command output or prompts. Transcripts
are backed up before compaction to `.claude/data/transcript_backups/`,
owner-only. Both directories are git-ignored by `gingugu init`.
